      "message": "CFI breaks if the function pointer type for an indirect call doesn\u0027t match the target function type.\n\nThe type filler_t is primarily used for calling readpage from struct address_space_operations, where the type of the first parameter is struct file*. Unfortunately, filler_t is used also for other purposes, like here, where the first parameter is used for something completely different.\n\nThis changes fixes the build (with -Werror\u003dincompatible-pointer-types), but perhaps a better solution would be to not use filler_t here in the first place. However, that would be a more complicated change.",
